msgid ""
"The standard Davidson corrected correlation energies are defined as "
"\\begin{align}"
msgstr "标准的 Davidson 校正相关能定义为 \\begin{align}"

msgid ""
"where :math:`c_n` is the coefficient of the (fixed) reference function in "
"the MRCI wave function: \\begin{align}"
msgstr "其中 :math:`c_n` 是（固定的）参考函数在 MRCI 波函数中的系数：\\begin{align}"

msgid ""
"and the correlation energies are \\begin{align} E_{\\rm corr}^{(n)}=E_{\\rm "
"mrci}^{(n)}-E_{\\rm ref}^{(n)} .\\label{eq:ecorr}\\end{align} In the "
"vicinity of avoided crossings this correction may give unreasonable results "
"since the reference function may get a small overlap with the MRCI wave "
"function. One way to avoid this problem is to replace the reference wave "
"function :math:`\\Psi_{\\rm ref}^{(n)}` by the the relaxed reference "
"functions"
msgstr ""
"而相关能为 \\begin{align} E_{\\rm corr}^{(n)}=E_{\\rm mrci}^{(n)}-E_{\\rm "
"ref}^{(n)} .\\label{eq:ecorr}\\end{align} 在避免交叉附近，此校正可能给出不合理的结果，因为参考函数与 MRCI"
" 波函数的重叠可能很小。避免此问题的一种方法是用弛豫参考函数替代参考波函数 :math:`\\Psi_{\\rm ref}^{(n)}`"

msgid "which simply leads to \\begin{align}"
msgstr "这直接导致 \\begin{align}"

msgid ""
"\\end{align} Alternatively, one can linearly combine the fixed reference "
"functions to maximize the overlap with the MRCI wave functions. This yields "
"projected functions"
msgstr "\\end{align} 或者，可以将固定的参考函数线性组合，以最大化与 MRCI 波函数的重叠。由此得到投影函数"

msgid "Thus, in this case we use for the Davidson correction \\begin{align}"
msgstr "因此，在这种情况下，我们对 Davidson 修正使用 \\begin{align}"

msgid ""
"\\end{align} The final question is which reference energy to use to compute "
"the correlation energy used in eq. \\eqref{eq:dav}. In older MOLPRO version "
"(to 2009.1) the reference wave function which has the largest overlap with "
"the MRCI wave function was used to compute the reference energy for the "
"corresponding state. But this can lead to steps of the Davidson corrected "
"energies if the order of the states swaps along potential energy functions. "
"In this version there are two options: the default is to use for state "
":math:`n` the reference energy :math:`n`, cf. eq. \\eqref{eq:ecorr} "
"(assuming the states are ordered according to increasing energy). The second"
" option is to recompute the correlation energies using the rotated reference"
" functions \\begin{align} E_{corr}^{(n)} &=& E_{\\rm MRCI}^{(n)} - \\langle "
"\\Psi_{\\rm rot}^{(n)} \\| \\hat H \\|  \\Psi_{\\rm rot}^{(n)} \\rangle  "
"\\label{eq:erot}\\end{align} Both should give smooth potentials (unless at "
"conical intersections or crossings of states with different symmetries), but"
" there is no guarantee that the Davidson corrected energies of different "
"states don’t cross. This problem is unavoidable for non-variational "
"energies. The relaxed and rotated Davidson corrections give rather similar "
"results; the rotated one yields somewhat larger cluster corrections and was "
"found to give better results in the case of the F + H\\ :math:`_2` potential"
" [see `J. Chem. Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.2822905>`__ **128**, "
"034305 (2008)]."
msgstr ""
"\\end{align} 最后一个问题是使用哪个参考能量来计算式 \\eqref{eq:dav} 中使用的相关能。在较老的 MOLPRO 版本（至 "
"2009.1）中，使用与 MRCI 波函数重叠最大的参考波函数来计算相应态的参考能量。但如果沿势能函数态的次序发生交换，这可能导致 Davidson "
"修正能量出现跳变。在此版本中有两个选项：默认情况下，对态 :math:`n` 使用参考能量 :math:`n`\\ ，参见式 "
"\\eqref{eq:ecorr}（假设态按能量递增排列）。第二个选项是使用旋转后的参考函数重新计算相关能 \\begin{align} "
"E_{corr}^{(n)} &=& E_{\\rm MRCI}^{(n)} - \\langle \\Psi_{\\rm rot}^{(n)} \\|"
" \\hat H \\|  \\Psi_{\\rm rot}^{(n)} \\rangle  \\label{eq:erot}\\end{align} "
"两者都应给出光滑的势（除非在锥形交叉处或不同对称性态的交叉处），但不能保证不同态的 Davidson "
"修正能量不会交叉。对于非变分能量，这个问题不可避免。弛豫的 Davidson 修正和旋转的 Davidson "
"修正给出相当类似的结果；旋转的修正给出稍大的簇修正，并被发现在 F + H\\ :math:`_2` 势的情况下给出更好的结果 [见 `J. Chem."
" Phys. <https://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.2822905>`__ **128**, 034305 (2008)]。"

